Package: vex-timer
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: E-Vex <raiedaleve@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/E-Vex/vex-cli-study-timer
Description: Command-line study timer with chiptune alarms and desktop notifications
 Vex CLI Study Timer schedules focus sessions and breaks, draws a live
 progress display, and plays a synthesized chiptune alarm when a phase
 completes. Sessions, focus, break, and long-break cadence are all
 configurable, and timing is drift-resistant absolute CLOCK_MONOTONIC
 deadline tracking.
 .
 The binary is statically linked, so the package has no shared-library
 dependencies. Sound playback additionally uses aplay from alsa-utils and
 desktop notifications use notify-send from libnotify-bin (both optional).
Suggests: alsa-utils, libnotify-bin
